<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Genghis Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1162–<a href="/years/1227">1227</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Chinggis Khan, Temüjin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Genghis Khan, born Temüjin in 1162, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>. Uniting the Mongol tribes in 1206, he launched conquests across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, including the destruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>. His descendants ruled successor states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a>, and his legacy was claimed by later rulers, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/genghis-khan.jpg" alt="Genghis Khan" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YuanEmperorAlbumGenghisPortrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
